From 9ef4731607decca4a5d99fe9d7bfb83ff5c792ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:46:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] job-cancel: POST /job/run/{run_id}/cancel stops a run now and
 frees its session

The headset stops following a run when the user switches to another scanned model mid-run (the
app's switchclean lane). Until now the server's run went on for minutes (a replace's search cap is
150 s, its model waits 60 s more), and every new job for that session got "a job is already
running; give it a moment".

- runjob.Run keeps its chain task (and a replace run's next-model builds) in `tasks`.
- runjob.cancel(run, reason): marks the run `cancelled`, every unfinished step `cancelled`, closes
  its actions with job_done {run_id, status: "cancelled", kind, reason?}, and cancels its tasks
  at the await they are in (a search / model / LLM wait). The session may start a new job at once
  (register's Busy check only counts running runs). Idempotent: an ended run is left alone.
- Both chains write nothing after a cancel (a step that swallowed the cancel adds no job_step, no
  actions, no second job_done); the replace chain cancels its next-model builds (st.others).
  Background jobs a step started (a search in the jobs table) finish on their own (shared cache).
- POST /job/run/{run_id}/cancel {session_id?, reason?} (async: task.cancel() on the loop):
  404 unknown run, 403 another session's run, else {run_id, status, cancelled, next}.
- tests/test_job_cancel.py: a replace waiting on its search (the session starts a new job at
  once; no place_part; one job_done), its next-model builds, idempotence + 404, 403, and a whole
  job run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
